    "title": "Sourcer Private Destinations",
    "company": "Royal Caribbean Group",
    "location": "Remote",
    "description": "<strong>Journey with us!</strong> Combine your career goals and sense of adventure by joining our incredible team of employees at <strong>Royal Caribbean Group</strong>. We are proud to offer a competitive compensation and benefits package, and excellent career development opportunities, each offering unique ways to explore the world.<br><br>We are proud to be the vacation-industry leader with global brands â including Royal Caribbean International, Celebrity Cruises and Silversea Cruises â the most innovative fleet and private destinations, and the best people. Together, we are dedicated to turning the vacation of a lifetime into a lifetime of vacations for our guests.<br><br>Royal Caribbean Groupâs <strong>Shipboard Recruiting team</strong> has an exciting career opportunity for a full time <strong>Sourcer, Private Destinations</strong> reporting to the <strong>Director, Shipboard Recruiting</strong>.<br><br><strong>This position will reside in Nassau Bahamas and will sit in our main office.<br><br></strong><strong>Position Summary<br><br></strong>The Sourcer executes all strategic sourcing activities in partnership with the Private Destinations talent acquisition initiatives across entry levels and functions.<br><br>The goal is to ensure that the organization can consistently proactively deploy the right people, in the right place, at the right time, at the most efficient cost, and for them to be fully engaged.<br><br><strong>Essential Duties And Responsibilities<br><br></strong><ul><li>Builds and implements sourcing strategy.</li><li>Understands and executes current trends and best practices in sourcing and talent attraction.</li><li>Builds talent pipelines from various platforms such as social media, job boards, niche sites, and other similar platforms to implement sourcing strategy.</li><li>Creates candidate pipeline ahead of need and real time.</li><li>Leverages proprietary pipelines of candidates through our ATS and CRM.</li><li>Collaborates with recruiters to develop market strategy, pipeline candidates, provide insights, and share competitive intelligence.</li><li>Partners with the necessary team(s) to establish, develop, and maintain relationships with hiring managers.</li><li>Provides support of inbound sourcing (candidate / req management) as needed.</li><li>Assists with recruitment marketing and events initiatives.</li><li>Help support candidates with applications.</li><li>Assists with overseeing Smartsheet trackers.</li><li>Meets operational business goals and KPIâs.<br><br></li></ul><strong>Qualifications<br><br></strong><ul><li>Bachelorâs degree in human resource management, business administration, or related field from an accredited college or university or the international equivalent required.</li><li>Minimum two (2) yearsâ experience in working for a global/international or reputable local organization in the same capacity.</li><li>Working knowledge of computers, internet access, and the ability to navigate within an automated HRIS system as well as variety software packages such as Excel, Word, and PowerPoint; familiar with social media and relevant company/brand efforts.</li><li>Good working knowledge in recruitment strategies and talent pool management</li><li>Knowledge of accepted human resources practices and the laws governing employment and fair treatment of employees globally.</li><li>Must be tactful, resolute, and committed to providing excellent customer service.</li><li>Must have a flexible approach to change, is able to work effectively in a variety of situations, seeks improvements and looks to the future.</li><li>Strong written and presentational skills; ability to clearly communicate complex messages to a variety of audiences including management.</li><li>Ability to work with colleagues, managers, and stakeholders in effective partnership.<br><br></li></ul><strong>We know there's a lot to consider.</strong> As you go through the application process, our recruiters will be glad to provide guidance, and more relevant details to answer any additional questions. Thank you again for your interest in Royal Caribbean Group. We'll hope to see you onboard soon!<br><br>It is the policy of the Company to ensure equal employment and promotion opportunity to qualified candidates without discrimination or harassment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, sexual orientation, sexuality, gender identity or expression, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Royal Caribbean Group and each of its subsidiaries prohibit and will not tolerate discrimination or harassment.<br/><br/>Please mention the word **HARMLESS** and tag ROTguOTcuNzYuODU= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#ROTguOTcuNzYuODU=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.",
