    "title": "Store Manager Bunbury",
    "company": "Retail FX",
    "location": "Remote",
    "description": "Our client, a leading international women's fashion retailer, is seeking an experienced Store Manager to lead one of their high-performing stores. With a growing presence across Australia and New Zealand, the brand is known for its fashion-led styling and curated collections across apparel, accessories, swimwear, shapewear, and activewear. This is an opportunity to lead a passionate team focused on customer experience and styling.<br><br><strong>Exciting Leadership Opportunity in Women's Fashion!<br><br></strong><strong>What's In It For You<br><br></strong><ul><li>Competitive base salary of up to $68,000 + Super + Discounts + Incentives</li><li>Opportunities for career growth and advancement</li><li>Generous staff discounts on fashion-forward products</li><li>Ongoing training and professional support</li><li>Tuesday to Saturday roster</li><li>Recognition and rewards for your outstanding contributions<br><br></li></ul><strong>The Role<br><br></strong>As the Manager, you'll be at the forefront of driving sales, exceeding company KPIs, and inspiring a talented sales team. We need a go-getter who thrives working independently and loves styling up a storm. Your responsibilities will include:<br><br><ul><li>Leading and motivating your team to achieve and surpass sales goals</li><li>Building and maintaining strong relationships with customers, offering personalised styling advice</li><li>Implementing visual merchandising standards to create an engaging and inspiring store environment</li><li>Training and developing your team to ensure exceptional service and performance</li><li>Being the face of the store, providing a memorable shopping experience for every client<br><br></li></ul><strong>Skills &amp; Requirements<br><br></strong><ul><li>2-3 years of experience in retail management, ideally in apparel</li><li>A proven ability to deliver personalised styling experiences and a love for styling up a storm</li><li>Strong communication skills </li><li>Previo