  {
    "id": "remoteok-1137212",
    "source": "RemoteOK",
    "title": "Building Maintenance Technician",
    "company": "Dart",
    "location": "Remote",
    "description": "<p><strong>JOB TITLE:</strong> Building Maintenance Technician</p><p><br></p><p><strong>SALARY:</strong> CI$50,000 - CI$70,000 pa</p><p><br></p><p><strong>WORKING HOURS: </strong>40 HOURS PER WEEK</p><p><br></p><p><strong>TERM OF EMPLOYMENT</strong>: Full-Time</p><p><br></p><p>We are seeking a Building Maintenance Technician to join our team. The successful candidate will be responsible for the inspection, maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of building infrastructure and systems to ensure safe, reliable, and efficient operation of facilities.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>DO YOU HAVE:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>A high school diploma (or equivalent) and a valid trade license</p><p>A minimum of 5 yearsâ experience in building maintenance within Class A Commercial properties</p><p>Strong HVAC experience in chilled water and DX systems</p><p>Training and certification in electrical, plumbing, HVAC systems maintenance, Pool Operator and Man Lift operation</p><p>A valid Cayman Islands driverâs license</p><p>The ability to operate hand and power tools required, in a safe and efficient manner</p><p>Strong knowledge of building, electrical, plumbing and MEP systems, including related equipment, tools, hazards and safety precautions</p><p>Strong communication, problem-solving, and troubleshooting skills</p><p>The ability to perform physically demanding manual work for extended periods in varying and sometimes adverse conditions is required, including working in inclement weather and with regular exposure to dust and noise, as well as heavy lifting, prolonged standing, and climbing</p><p>The willingness to travel between sites, work at heights, and work outside regular business hours as required</p><p>The ability to read and interpret schematic drawings and blueprints (preferred)</p><p>A commitment to safety, continuous improvement, and professional development</p><p><br></p><p><strong>WE WANT YOU TO:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Inspect, maintain, troubleshoot, and repair mechanical, electrical, plumbing, fire life safety, and other building systems</p><p>Diagnose faults using schematic drawings, manuals, and blueprints, and complete corrective maintenance efficiently</p><p>Assess faulty equipment, determine repair or replacement needs, review manufacturer specifications and technical documentation, and source the required parts or materials</p><p>Adhere to the DE Engineering Health and Safety Manual and maintain accurate maintenance records</p><p>Respond to corrective maintenance requests and urgent faults, diagnosing root causes and completing repairs effectively</p><p>Inspect and maintain building exteriors, residential units, appliances, fixtures, pools, and site features</p><p>Inspect, operate, maintain, and repair HVAC, solar systems, lighting, and related building systems while identifying performance issues and implementing system upgrades as required</p><p>Support contractor coordination, disaster preparedness, and recovery activities</p><p>Communicate effectively, work collaboratively, promote a safe customer-focused environment, and demonstrate professionalism and sound judgment</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits</strong></p><p><br></p><p>At Dart, we're committed to creating a workplace where you thrive, offering a competitive salary and benefits designed for your well-being and growth. Our package includes 100% employer-paid medical insurance premium for the employee, employee and employer pension contributions, life insurance and long-term disability coverage (conditions apply), enhanced leave options including vacation, personal days, maternity, paternity, a wellness screening day and continuing professional development opportunities after successful completion of a six-month probationary period.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>DEADLINE:</strong> Midnight, Friday 18 September 2026.</p><p><br></p><br/><br/>Please mention the word **TERRIFIC** and tag RMjYwNTo1OWMwOmUzZjo3MTA4OjU4M2Q6NDQ5Yzo4ZmE6MmJlMw== when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwNTo1OWMwOmUzZjo3MTA4OjU4M2Q6NDQ5Yzo4ZmE6MmJlMw==). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.",
