  {
    "id": "wwr-84d843489dbb",
    "source": "We Work Remotely",
    "title": "Sedona Digital: Senior Platform Engineer(DevOps)",
    "company": "",
    "location": "Remote (Worldwide)",
    "description": "\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Headquarters:</strong> Romania\n</p>\n\n<p>Join&nbsp;Sedona Digital,&nbsp;a fast-growing scale-up organization with an ambition to be recognized as one of the leading technology companies servicing high tech, global enterprises across&nbsp;Technology, Finance, and Life Sciences sectors. Our global client base needs builders: engineers and developers who love technology, have deep&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;in software, engineering, and cloud technologies, and importantly, have a passion for culture and customers. &nbsp;</p><ul><li>We obsess&nbsp;about&nbsp;our customers &nbsp;</li><li>We build outstanding technical solutions </li><li>We create an awesome culture &nbsp;</li><li>We accelerate learning and careers &nbsp;</li></ul><p>As a&nbsp;Senior Platform Engineer, you will join a team who&nbsp;strive&nbsp;to push cloud services to the&nbsp;maximum&nbsp;limit every day using&nbsp;cutting-edge&nbsp;technologies. We are looking for a highly self-motivated&nbsp;professional&nbsp;who embraces DevOps culture, has experience with AWS services and technologies and is passionate about learning, automating,&nbsp;innovating&nbsp;and working in a highly collaborative environment.&nbsp;</p><p></p><p><strong>Your activities will include:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Initiate and actively drive the adoption of good patterns,&nbsp;structures&nbsp;and use of technologies for development and operations&nbsp;</li><li>Investigate and&nbsp;identify&nbsp;practices and work that can&nbsp;benefit&nbsp;from automation&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Monitor and suggest improvements to the existing CI/CD process to increase speed,&nbsp;safety&nbsp;and reliability&nbsp;</li><li>Implement and coordinate implementation with the parties involved&nbsp;</li><li>Develop and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;existing /GitLab CI pipeline libraries&nbsp;</li><li>Assist&nbsp;developers with setting up CI/CD for their projects and provide support for any issues that may arise&nbsp;</li><li>Stay up to date with the latest tools and trends in the industry&nbsp;</li><li>Provide senior-level, best practice recommendations and implementations to our Windows,&nbsp;Linux&nbsp;and Kubernetes hosting environments&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Function as a mentor to junior team members,&nbsp;providing&nbsp;technical guidance and recommending continued learning opportunities to help them develop&nbsp;</li><li>Educate fellow team members as well as Application Development Teams about the platforms&nbsp;used-for&nbsp;and&nbsp;hosted-by&nbsp;our team. Key tools and concepts in this space are: Gitlab, Docker, AWS, Terraform, Istio Service&nbsp;Mesh,&nbsp; Kubernetes&nbsp;, Kafka, ELK&nbsp;</li><li>Work with our Security team to remediate high-risk vulnerabilities and ensure the security of our environments are being&nbsp;scrutinized&nbsp;as&nbsp;appropriate for&nbsp;their use case&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Offer services related to the above tasks and projects to any of the Companies of the Group as instructed by the Line Manager&nbsp;</li></ul> <ul><li>University degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a similar discipline&nbsp;</li><li><strong>7+ years’ experience</strong> within the following areas: <strong>Cloud&nbsp;( AWS), Release Pipeline Management, Windows Server Administration, Linux Administration, Certificate Management, PowerShell scripting, Bash/python scripting, Configuration Management and IAC (Ansible/Terraform), DNS, Networking&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></li><li>Enterprise-level <strong>Kubernetes </strong>experience&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Solid <strong>Linux</strong> administration skills&nbsp;</li><li>Commitment to continuous improvement, with a focus on observability, modern application architecture styles,&nbsp;blue-green&nbsp;/ canary deployments, <strong>CI/CD pipeline management</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Ability to self-motivate, study, and stay&nbsp;on-top&nbsp;of emerging technologies and trends, while meeting business deadlines&nbsp;</li><li>Experience with tools including: <strong>Istio, Prometheus, Grafana, ELK, MSK, New Relic</strong>&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Bonus Points: What Will Make You Stand Out   &nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Familiarity with database concepts&nbsp;</li><li>Working experience with at least one cloud provider (preferably AWS)</li><li>Experience with Apache Kafka configuration and troubleshooting&nbsp;</li><li>Experience with ELK configuration and troubleshooting</li><li>Scripting skills (Bash, PowerShell, Python, Go, etc.) &nbsp;</li></ul> <ul><li>Work from home&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Medical insurance given after probation period&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Training on market trends and client needs&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Continuous learning and personal development opportunities&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Holiday allowance in line with local legislation&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Competitive compensation package&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Performance - based bonus&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Fun budget for team events &nbsp;</li></ul>\n\n<p><strong>To apply:</strong> <a href=\"https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/sedona-digital-senior-platform-engineer-devops\">https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/sedona-digital-senior-platform-engineer-devops</a></p>\n",
