  {
    "id": "himalayas-5a4c78bcbe0d",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "WordPress Developer",
    "company": "",
    "location": "Pakistan",
    "description": "<h3><strong>WordPress Developer (Elementor, WooCommerce, SEO &amp; Performance Optimization) – Remote</strong></h3><p><strong>Position Type:</strong> Full-Time, Remote<br><strong>Working Hours:</strong> U.S. Client Business Hours</p><h3><strong>About the Role</strong></h3><p>At <a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/pavago\">Pavago</a>, we’re hiring a skilled <strong>WordPress Developer</strong> for one of our clients to build, optimize, and maintain modern, responsive, and high-performing WordPress websites.</p><p>This is a hands-on development role for someone who combines strong <strong>WordPress, PHP, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript skills</strong> with an understanding of website performance, SEO, user experience, and conversion-focused design.</p><p>You’ll work across website builds, landing pages, WooCommerce functionality, performance optimization, plugin integrations, security, and ongoing maintenance while collaborating with marketing, design, and content teams.</p><p>If you enjoy building WordPress websites that are <strong>fast, secure, responsive, and built to perform</strong>, this role is a strong fit.</p><h3><strong>What You’ll Own</strong></h3><h3><strong>WordPress Development</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>Build and customize WordPress websites using:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Elementor</li>\n<li>Divi</li>\n<li>WPBakery</li>\n<li>Custom themes</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Develop landing pages, blogs, marketing websites, business websites, and WooCommerce stores.</li>\n<li>Create reusable templates and scalable page structures.</li>\n<li>Build and maintain custom and child themes.</li>\n<li>Customize functionality using PHP, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.</li>\n<li>Ensure websites are structured for long-term scalability and easy maintenance.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>Frontend Development &amp; User Experience</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>Convert Figma, Adobe XD, or Sketch designs into responsive WordPress pages.</li>\n<li>Build polished layouts across desktop, tablet, and mobile.</li>\n<li>Ensure cross-browser compatibility and responsive behavior.</li>\n<li>Follow accessibility and modern UX best practices.</li>\n<li>Improve site navigation, usability, and overall customer experience.</li>\n<li>Build conversion-focused pages that support marketing and business objectives.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>Website Performance &amp; Core Web Vitals</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>Optimize websites for speed and performance.</li>\n<li>Improve Core Web Vitals and Lighthouse scores.</li>\n<li>Implement:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Caching</li>\n<li>Lazy loading</li>\n<li>Image compression</li>\n<li>Code minification</li>\n<li>CDN integrations</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Run performance audits using:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Google Lighthouse</li>\n<li>GTmetrix</li>\n<li>PageSpeed Insights</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Identify and resolve performance bottlenecks across plugins, themes, scripts, and hosting environments.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>SEO Optimization</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>Implement technical and on-page SEO best practices.</li>\n<li>Configure and manage tools such as:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Yoast SEO</li>\n<li>Rank Math</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Optimize metadata, heading structures, images, URLs, and internal site structure.</li>\n<li>Support schema implementation and structured data.</li>\n<li>Collaborate with marketing and content teams on SEO-focused improvements.</li>\n<li>Ensure website updates do not negatively affect search visibility or performance.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>WooCommerce, Plugins &amp; Integrations</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>Install, configure, and customize WordPress plugins.</li>\n<li>Support WooCommerce stores and e-commerce functionality.</li>\n<li>Work with plugins such as:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Elementor Pro</li>\n<li>Contact Form 7</li>\n<li>Yoast SEO</li>\n<li>Membership plugins</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Troubleshoot plugin conflicts and compatibility issues.</li>\n<li>Extend plugin or website functionality using PHP when required.</li>\n<li>Integrate third-party marketing, CRM, analytics, and business tools.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>Security &amp; Website Maintenance</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>Manage WordPress core, plugin, and theme updates.</li>\n<li>Implement security best practices using tools such as Wordfence, Sucuri, or iThemes Security.</li>\n<li>Configure backups, staging environments, and disaster recovery processes.</li>\n<li>Monitor website health and uptime.</li>\n<li>Troubleshoot bugs, broken layouts, hosting issues, and technical errors.</li>\n<li>Maintain stable and secure production environments.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>Collaboration &amp; Deployment</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>Work closely with marketing, design, content, and development teams.</li>\n<li>Support landing pages and website updates for marketing campaigns.</li>\n<li>Provide CMS support to non-technical team members.</li>\n<li>Test changes before production deployment.</li>\n<li>Push updates through staging and deployment workflows.</li>\n<li>Maintain organized documentation and development processes.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>What Makes You a Strong Fit</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>You have strong hands-on WordPress development experience.</li>\n<li>You can work beyond page builders when custom development is required.</li>\n<li>You care about website speed, responsiveness, usability, and technical quality.</li>\n<li>You can translate designs into polished, production-ready pages.</li>\n<li>You’re comfortable diagnosing plugin, theme, hosting, and performance issues.</li>\n<li>You understand how development decisions affect SEO and conversions.</li>\n<li>You take ownership of website quality from development through deployment.</li>\n<li>You work effectively and independently in a remote environment.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>Required Experience &amp; Skills</strong></h3><ul>\n<li><strong>2+ years of professional WordPress development experience.</strong></li>\n<li>Strong proficiency with:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>WordPress</li>\n<li>PHP</li>\n<li>HTML</li>\n<li>CSS</li>\n<li>JavaScript</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Hands-on experience with Elementor, Divi, WPBakery, or similar page builders.</li>\n<li>Experience with custom themes and child themes.</li>\n<li>Strong understanding of responsive and mobile-first development.</li>\n<li>Experience with website speed and Core Web Vitals optimization.</li>\n<li>Understanding of technical and on-page SEO.</li>\n<li>Experience managing hosting environments such as:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>WP Engine</li>\n<li>SiteGround</li>\n<li>Kinsta</li>\n<li>cPanel</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Strong troubleshooting and debugging abilities.</li>\n<li>Ability to work during U.S. client business hours.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>WooCommerce development and customization experience.</li>\n<li>Experience building or modifying custom WordPress plugins.</li>\n<li>Familiarity with Git and CI/CD workflows.</li>\n<li>Experience managing staging and production environments.</li>\n<li>Experience with APIs, CRM integrations, or marketing automation tools.</li>\n<li>Background supporting SaaS companies, agencies, e-commerce brands, or marketing teams.</li>\n<li>Understanding of conversion rate optimization (CRO).</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>What a Typical Day Looks Like</strong></h3><h3>Your day may include:</h3><ul>\n<li>Reviewing website support requests and technical issues.</li>\n<li>Building a new landing page from a Figma design.</li>\n<li>Customizing WordPress themes or functionality.</li>\n<li>Optimizing page speed and Core Web Vitals.</li>\n<li>Troubleshooting plugin conflicts or responsive layout issues.</li>\n<li>Supporting a marketing campaign or website launch.</li>\n<li>Implementing SEO improvements.</li>\n<li>Applying WordPress, plugin, and security updates.</li>\n<li>Testing changes within a staging environment.</li>\n<li>Deploying approved updates to production.</li>\n</ul><p><strong>In short:</strong> you ensure WordPress websites are fast, secure, scalable, visually polished, and optimized for both users and business performance.</p><h3><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>Websites consistently load in <strong>under 3 seconds</strong>.</li>\n<li>Strong Core Web Vitals and Lighthouse performance scores.</li>\n<li>Fast turnaround on website updates and support requests.</li>\n<li>Minimal website downtime and security incidents.</li>\n<li>Responsive, polished, and conversion-focused website builds.</li>\n<li>Reliable WordPress, plugin, and theme maintenance.</li>\n<li>Reduced recurring technical and performance issues.</li>\n<li>Positive feedback from marketing, content, and design teams.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>Why This Role Stands Out</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>Work across modern WordPress websites and marketing campaigns.</li>\n<li>Strong ownership and autonomy over development work.</li>\n<li>Build high-performing and conversion-focused digital experiences.</li>\n<li>Work across WordPress development, WooCommerce, SEO, UX, and performance optimization.</li>\n<li>Collaborate directly with marketing, design, and content teams.</li>\n<li>Fully remote environment with U.S.-based collaboration.</li>\n<li>Growth opportunities into <strong>Senior WordPress Developer, Web Development Lead, or Technical Web Specialist</strong> roles.</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>Interview Process</strong></h3><ul>\n<li>Initial Phone Screen</li>\n<li>Video Interview with <a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/pavago\">Pavago</a> Recruiter</li>\n<li>Practical Assessment:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Build a landing page from Figma <strong>or</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Optimize a WordPress demo website</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Client Interview</li>\n<li>Offer &amp; Background Verification</li>\n</ul><h3><strong>What Happens After You Apply</strong></h3><p>Right after you apply, you’ll receive an email invitation from <strong>Spark Hire</strong> to record your <strong>Intro Video</strong>. It’s a short, self-recorded video completed on your own time, and it’s the final step that completes your application.</p><p>Instead of repeating yourself across multiple screening calls, you get to introduce yourself once and let your story carry forward. Hiring managers can see how you communicate before meeting you, making future interviews more focused and meaningful.</p><p>You can record your video as many times as you like before submitting it — only your final submission will be reviewed.</p><p>Please keep an eye on both your <strong>inbox and spam folder</strong> for your Spark Hire invitation.</p><h3><strong>Apply Now</strong></h3><p>If you’re an experienced WordPress Developer who enjoys <strong>building polished websites, solving technical problems, improving performance, and optimizing for SEO and conversions</strong>, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p>Apply today and help build WordPress experiences that are fast, secure, responsive, and designed to perform.</p><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
