  {
    "id": "himalayas-6967dac07d9d",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "Wordpress Developer (Remote or NYC-Based)",
    "company": "",
    "location": "United States",
    "description": "Category: Internet Services <br><br>Location: <br><br><br><div>Dignotion is looking for an experienced and detail-oriented <b>WordPress Developer</b> to support a range of high-impact web projects. This is a remote, project-based opportunity with flexible hours, ideal for developers who are comfortable working independently and bringing custom, performance-optimized WordPress solutions to life. <br>\n</div><div>In this role, you’ll work on both new builds and existing properties, including the development of feature-rich, fast-loading websites. Many of our projects involve complex content structures, dynamic listings, and third-party integrations—so strong experience with custom development beyond basic theming is essential.<br>\n</div><div>\n<b>Key Responsibilities</b><br>\n</div><ul>\n<li>Develop, customize, and maintain WordPress websites (themes, plugins, custom features) <br>\n</li>\n<li>Build pages from scratch with and without page builders (e.g. Elementor)<br>\n</li>\n<li>Optimize websites for performance, Web Core Vitals, and mobile responsiveness<br>\n</li>\n<li>Manage and monitor bug tracking, QA, and ongoing maintenance<br>\n</li>\n<li>Implement both backend and frontend features to spec<br>\n</li>\n<li>Support WooCommerce development and optimization<br>\n</li>\n<li>Improve site speed via caching, lazy loading, and optimized code<br>\n</li>\n<li>Configure complex hosting setups, load balancers, and Git-based version control<br>\n</li>\n<li>Integrate third-party APIs and dynamic content<br>\n</li>\n<li>Translate project briefs into development roadmaps and deliverables<br>\n</li>\n<li>Coordinate with internal teams and plugin/theme developers when needed<br><br>\n</li>\n</ul><br><h3>Requirements</h3><ul>\n<li>3+ years of hands-on WordPress development experience <br>\n</li>\n<li>Strong skills in HTML, CSS, PHP, MySQL, JavaScript, and related toolkits<br>\n</li>\n<li>Experience working with REST APIs (advantage)<br>\n</li>\n<li>Familiarity with Git workflows and version control (advantage)<br>\n</li>\n<li>Understanding of cross-browser compatibility and responsive design<br>\n</li>\n<li>Ability to plan structured, scalable builds and follow through independently<br>\n</li>\n<li>Excellent communication and fluent written English<br>\n</li>\n<li>Experience working remotely and managing tasks asynchronously<br>\n</li>\n<li>Familiarity with page builders like Elementor (advantage)<br>\n</li>\n<li>Experience with affiliate marketing tools or link tracking (advantage)<br>\n</li>\n</ul><div>\n<b>Additional Bonus Points If You Have:</b><ul>\n<li>Prior work developing listing-based, comparison, or directory-style websites <br>\n</li>\n<li>Comfort working with structured content, advanced filtering, and UX-driven data presentation<br>\n</li>\n<li>Experience creating CMS-driven experiences tailored for performance and scalability<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<br><h3>Benefits</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fully remote or hybrid work (NYC-based optional) <br>\n</li>\n<li>Flexible working hours and project scope<br>\n</li>\n<li>Competitive rates, defined individually per project and experience level<br>\n</li>\n<li>Opportunity to work on technically challenging, high-visibility builds with a skilled and collaborative team<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<br><br><br><br>Details</div><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
