    "id": "himalayas-d5592632b85c",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "[Pooling] Software Engineer - PHP",
    "company": "",
    "location": "United States",
    "description": "<p>We are seeking a proactive and experienced <strong>PHP Software Engineer</strong> to support a fast-paced migration project. You will join our backend engineering team and work closely with cross-functional stakeholders to upgrade legacy systems to the latest PHP version. This is a critical initiative with tight deadlines, and we are looking for someone who can jump in immediately, take ownership, and deliver high-quality solutions quickly.</p><h3>Key Responsibilities:</h3><ul>\n<li>Collaborate with the clients technical team to understand the current system architecture and migration goals.</li>\n<li>Assist in upgrading the PHP codebase to the latest stable version, ensuring compatibility and performance improvements.</li>\n<li>Refactor and optimize existing PHP code, adhering to modern development standards and best practices.</li>\n<li>Conduct thorough testing and debugging to ensure system stability post-migration.</li>\n<li>Provide documentation and knowledge transfer as needed to ensure seamless handover.</li>\n<li>Work within a sprint-based agile environment, delivering high-quality results under tight deadlines.</li>\n</ul><h3>Qualifications:</h3><ul>\n<li>Hands-on experience with PHP (preferably PHP 7.x and 8.x).</li>\n<li>Strong understanding of object-oriented programming and modern PHP frameworks (Laravel, Symfony, etc.).</li>\n<li>Experience working with legacy PHP systems and performing version migrations.</li>\n<li>Familiarity with front-end integration and RESTful API development.</li>\n<li>Proficient in Git, CI/CD pipelines, and working in a collaborative Git-based environment.</li>\n<li>Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work independently or within a distributed team.</li>\n</ul><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
