    "id": "himalayas-1ee7091fe4a1",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "Senior PHP Developer Symfony",
    "company": "",
    "location": "United States",
    "description": "<p><strong>PHP Back-End Developer (Senior) - EdTech</strong>﻿﻿</p><p>A leading platform in educational center management, designed to simplify administrative and academic processes. We help our clients optimize their time, allowing them to focus on what truly matters: education.</p><p>we not only create innovative technology, but we also offer an environment where you can grow professionally, face exciting challenges, and be part of a team that is transforming the way educational centers manage their operations.</p><p>If you're looking for a company where you can contribute and evolve, this is the place for you.</p><p>We are looking for a Senior PHP Back-End Developer to join our team and help make <b>our product</b> more robust and scalable. You will work on resolving support tickets, continuous improvement of the platform, and developing new key functionalities. Additionally, we are looking for someone who can bring a strategic vision and have an impact on the technical decisions of the team, taking on additional responsibilities in defining and evolving the product's architecture.</p><h3>Key Responsibilities:</h3><ul>\n<li>Diagnose and solve problems in a dynamic, multi-platform development environment.</li>\n<li>Lead important technical initiatives and help define long-term technology strategy.</li>\n<li>Actively participate in resolving support tickets and continuous improvement.</li>\n<li>Develop and enhance functionalities, working alongside the team to ensure code quality and scalability.</li>\n<li>Propose innovative solutions to complex technical problems and anticipate the platform's future needs.</li>\n<li>Collaborate with other teams to ensure technical alignment with business needs.</li>\n<li>Effectively document development and key technical decisions.</li>\n<li>Communicate clearly and effectively both verbally and in writing in Spanish and English.</li>\n</ul><h3>Minimum Requirements:</h3><ul>\n<li>Over 5 years of professional experience in backend development with PHP (version 7 or higher).</li>\n<li>Solid experience with relational databases like MySQL or PostgreSQL.</li>\n<li>Advanced knowledge of the Symfony framework (versions 3-4 or higher).</li>\n<li>Experience with version control tools (Git).</li>\n<li>Analytical skills and the ability to solve complex problems.</li>\n<li>Excellent written and verbal communication skills in both Spanish and English.</li>\n</ul><h3>Desirable Requirements:</h3><ul>\n<li>Knowledge of JavaScript (especially frameworks like Angular, React, or jQuery).</li>\n<li>Experience working with AWS (Amazon Web Services).</li>\n<li>Familiarity with Elasticsearch.</li>\n<li>Experience with MySQL and NoSQL databases (MongoDB).</li>\n</ul><h3>We Offer:</h3><ul>\n<li>Dynamic and growing work environment.</li>\n<li>Remote, with possibility to go to the offices.</li>\n<li>Professional development opportunities within a motivated and expanding team.</li>\n</ul><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
