    "location": "United States",
    "description": "<h3>This is a remote position.</h3><p><b>Are you looking to be a part of an extraordinary Digital Transformation Company!</b></p><p><b>“We create sustainable solutions, as we take inspiration from the world around us and develop inventions”.</b></p><p>If you are an eager person for success, can see the invisible, and will go the extra mile to deliver the best, then you are, who we are looking for and we are offering <b>‘‘React Native Developer’’</b> role for you.</p><p>A brief job description of the position and preferred qualifications for the suitable candidates are defined below;</p><h3>Responsibilities:</h3><ul>\n<li>Ability to work through new and difficult React Native issues and contribute to libraries as needed,</li>\n<li>Alongside your full-stack development team, investigate technical feasibility and suggest implementation options,</li>\n<li>Work closely with key stakeholders such as Product Managers, UX Designers, and Quality Engineers,</li>\n<li>Contribute to our ongoing efforts to improve our processes and tools,</li>\n<li>Creating technical documentation for reference and reporting.</li>\n</ul><br><h3>Requirements</h3><h3>Qualifications:</h3><ul>\n<li>3+ years experience developing native Mobile Applications,</li>\n<li>Experience with React-Native,</li>\n<li>A strong understanding of JavaScript and/or TypeScript,</li>\n<li>A strong understanding of application architecture,</li>\n<li>Experience with RESTful APIs,</li>\n<li>Experience with client-side MVC/MVVM frameworks (e.g., Backbone, ReactJs),</li>\n<li>Constant focus on maintaining the quality of the code base and the customer experience,</li>\n<li>Strong analytical and debugging skills.</li>\n</ul><br><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
