  {
    "id": "himalayas-2a94cdddfe53",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "Senior React Developer",
    "company": "",
    "location": "United States",
    "description": "<h3>This is a remote position.</h3><h3><b>Why this role matters</b></h3><p>We’re building a next-generation SaaS platform used by thousands of professionals daily — and front-end experience is everything. From real-time dashboards to high-performance interfaces, we’re obsessed with usability and speed.</p><p>We’re hiring a <b>Senior React Developer</b> who cares deeply about user experience, clean architecture, and elegant code. You’ll take the lead on front-end features, collaborate closely with product and design, and help scale our platform as we grow fast.</p><h3>\n<b>What you’ll do</b><ul>\n<li><p>Build, test, and ship React components for complex, data-rich UIs</p></li>\n<li><p>Collaborate with designers to turn prototypes into real, pixel-perfect features</p></li>\n<li><p>Optimize performance for speed and scalability across browsers and devices</p></li>\n<li><p>Own the frontend architecture — refactor, modularize, and guide improvements</p></li>\n<li><p>Contribute to component libraries, design systems, and accessibility practices</p></li>\n<li><p>Review code, mentor teammates, and help raise the bar on front-end quality</p></li>\n<li><p>Work closely with backend engineers to integrate APIs and shape data flows</p></li>\n</ul>\n<br>\n</h3><h3>Requirements</h3><h3>\n<b>Who you are</b><ul>\n<li><p>4–6+ years of experience in frontend development with <b>deep React expertise</b></p></li>\n<li><p>Strong in <b>JavaScript (ES6+), TypeScript</b>, and front-end tooling (Webpack, Vite, etc.)</p></li>\n<li><p>Experience with <b>state management</b> (Redux, Zustand, Jotai, or similar)</p></li>\n<li><p>Comfortable working with <b>REST/GraphQL APIs</b> and async data handling</p></li>\n<li><p>Eye for detail in <b>UX/UI</b> and a bias for clean, maintainable code</p></li>\n<li><p>Proactive communicator who thrives in a collaborative product team</p></li>\n<li><p>Passionate about frontend performance, testing, and staying current with best practices</p></li>\n</ul>\n</h3><h3>\n<b>Nice to have</b><ul>\n<li><p>Experience in SaaS, B2B tools, or enterprise dashboards</p></li>\n<li><p>Familiarity with testing tools like Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress</p></li>\n</ul>\n<br>\n</h3><h3>Benefits</h3><h3>\n<b>Why join us</b><ul>\n<li><p>Build a product used daily by real customers, not vaporware</p></li>\n<li><p>A team that values code quality and developer experience</p></li>\n<li><p>Autonomy, zero micromanagement, and a supportive culture</p></li>\n<li><p>Competitive salary, equity options, and meaningful bonuses</p></li>\n<li><p>Flexible hours, remote-first setup, and a generous vacation policy</p></li>\n<li><p>Annual learning budget, wellness benefits, and real career growth</p></li>\n</ul>\n<br>\n</h3><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
