  {
    "id": "himalayas-3393cc432523",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "Full-Stack Web Developer",
    "company": "",
    "location": "Australia",
    "description": "<h3>Full-Stack Developer</h3><hr><p>Reach Game Studios is looking for a talented full-stack web developer to work on developing exciting new web presences across the studio portfolio: including game sites, backend web services infrastructure for our game titles, and corporate websites.</p><h3>Responsibilities:</h3><p>As a full-stack web developer you will be responsible for:</p><ul>\n<li>Working with designers and management to scope and implement elegant frontend web designs, or own the visual identity for projects.</li>\n<li>Creating backend game services infrastructure to serve our game, web, and interface requirements.</li>\n<li>Implementing endpoints and APIs to communicate between our front-end infrastructure, our community developers, and our game infrastructure.</li>\n<li>Work with game designers and engineers to expand our web services infrastructure as game requirements evolve.</li>\n<li>Implementing feature sets as required by a range of departments, particularly working with dev ops and live ops teams to ensure operation continuity.</li>\n</ul><h3>Requirements:</h3><h3>For this role we are looking for:</h3><ul>\n<li>An experienced front-end web developer with a demonstrated track record in effectively crafting responsive front-end web experiences.</li>\n<li>Knowledgable in web services development and endpoint development.</li>\n<li>A proven backend developer, including developing backend infrastructure, endpoints, and backend interfaces for internal use.</li>\n<li>High degree of practical and theoretical knowledge surrounding network and web security and a willingness to liaise and work with external partners to audit and ensure a high level of security across our web presences.</li>\n<li>Strong computer science fundamentals, including proficient across a number of languages and frameworks, data management and architecture.</li>\n<li>Proficient in C#, MVC Framework, Java, Javascript, NodeJS, C++, SQL, and a willingness to learn and interface with Unreal Engine for live game implementation.</li>\n<li>An understanding of online infrastructure, particularly surrounding live videogame web services.</li>\n</ul><h3>Remuneration:</h3><p>The position is currently a contract royalty-based position, with view to full-time employment post-launch. Contract amount is competitive and negotiable.</p><h3>Location:</h3><p>While we prioritize Australian/New Zealand applicants, we are a remote studio and consider international applications.</p><h3>Apply:</h3><p>To apply, please click on the \"Apply Now\" button below.</p><hr><div class=\"rbox-job-longdesc\"><p><em><a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/reach-game-studios-pty-ltd\">Reach Game Studios Pty. Ltd.</a> is a game development studio based in Sydney, Australia. Currently, the studio is working on action FPSRPG Glory. Reach Game Studios is a proudly diverse studio who value staff from all backgrounds and beliefs.</em></p></div><hr><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
