  {
    "id": "himalayas-4aa8e08e5b08",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "WordPress Web Developer (Elementor) - Freelance, Remote",
    "company": "",
    "location": "Philippines",
    "description": "<div><strong>About the Client</strong></div><div>Our client is a senior-led consulting firm specializing in enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems, helping mid-market finance and operations teams navigate growth, complexity, and ongoing system stewardship. They offer a mix of subscription-based support and outcome-based project delivery, working with finance teams that run multi-entity operations, complex billing models, and critical system integrations. The company has an established track record with recognizable mid-market and enterprise clients, and prides itself on senior-level expertise, clear documentation, and responsive service.</div><div>\n<div><strong>Why does this role exist?</strong></div>\n<div>This role exists because the client's internal team is currently stretched thin trying to maintain and update their WordPress/Elementor website themselves — leading to ad-hoc updates that take too long or don't get done, and real risk of breaking existing pages when non-specialists attempt changes. They need a dedicated, reliable specialist to own website updates and enhancements so the internal team no longer has to context-switch or fight with Elementor. This hire will become the go-to person for new sections, landing pages, and content publishing, working within the existing site to improve and extend it — not rebuild it.</div>\n<h3>The Impact you’ll make</h3>\n<div>\n<div><strong>Modify  Improve Existing Pages</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Update copy, imagery, sections, and layouts on existing WordPress pages</li>\n<li>Align new work with the existing design system and brand guidelines</li>\n<li>Implement updates without breaking current flows, layouts, or features</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>New Sections  Page Builds in Elementor</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Design and implement new sections and full pages inside Elementor</li>\n<li>Extend or duplicate existing layouts cleanly instead of reinventing structures</li>\n<li>Propose implementation options when requirements are loosely defined</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>Content Publishing  Maintenance</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Publish and format blog posts and other content updates</li>\n<li>Maintain the content library — remove outdated items, fix broken links, adjust navigation as needed</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>Quality, Stability  Responsiveness</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Ensure every change is fully responsive across desktop, tablet, and mobile</li>\n<li>Test updates to confirm no regressions or broken functionality</li>\n<li>Troubleshoot layout issues and minor front-end bugs related to page structure</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>Collaboration  Communication</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Collaborate with stakeholders to clarify requirements and communicate timelines clearly</li>\n<li>Proactively propose UX/layout improvements when opportunities are spotted</li>\n<li>Provide regular status updates, respond promptly during working hours, and flag blockers early</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>Skills, Knowledge and Expertise</h3>\n<div>\n<div><strong>Required:</strong></div>\n<ul><li>Strong, proven hands-on WordPress experience<br>Deep, hands-on Elementor experience — building new sections and editing/extending existing layouts<br>Solid understanding of responsive web design and mobile-first best practices<br>Ability to troubleshoot layout issues and minor front-end bugs related to page structure<br>Availability for at least 5 hours/week overlapping U.S. Eastern Time</li></ul>\n<div><strong>Your superpowers are...</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Technical Skills</strong><ul>\n<li>Deep, hands-on Elementor expertise (sections, layouts, cloning/extending existing structures)</li>\n<li>Strong general WordPress skills — comfortable working within an existing site rather than building from scratch</li>\n<li>Understanding of responsive/mobile-first design principles</li>\n<li>Ability to diagnose and fix minor front-end/layout bugs</li>\n<li>Working knowledge of on-page SEO basics (meta tags, alt text, internal linking) — a plus</li>\n<li>Comfort with light copy/layout refinement — headings, spacing, visual hierarchy — a plus</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Soft Skills</strong><ul>\n<li>Highly responsive and reliable — replies promptly and doesn't let requests go stale</li>\n<li>Detail-oriented, especially when it comes to not breaking what already works</li>\n<li>Strong written communicator who can give clear, concise async updates</li>\n<li>Comfortable interpreting loose requirements and proposing solutions rather than waiting for exact specs</li>\n<li>Proactive — flags blockers early rather than letting them sit</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>WFH Set-Up:</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Computer with at least 8GB RAM, an Intel i5 core processor/AMD Ryzen 5 Processor and up.</li>\n<li>Internet speed of at least 40MBPS</li>\n<li>Headset with an extended mic that has noise cancellation and a webcam</li>\n<li>Back-up computer and internet connection</li>\n<li>Quiet, dedicated workspace at home</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>You should apply if...</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>You're the kind of developer who respects an existing site instead of wanting to tear it down and start over. </li>\n<li>You take pride in shipping clean, stable updates — not just fast ones — and you double-check your work across devices before calling it done. </li>\n<li>You're comfortable being handed a loose brief (\"we need a new section here, make it work\") and turning that into a clear plan, a timeline, and a finished page. </li>\n<li>Communication isn't an afterthought for you — you proactively update people before they have to ask, and you flag problems before they become bigger ones. </li>\n<li>If you like the idea of being the trusted go-to person who keeps a site running smoothly and growing steadily, this role is built for you.</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>What to expect...<div><strong>Work Setup:</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Remote position</li>\n<li>Must have a reliable internet connection and a quiet workspace</li>\n<li>Required to provide own computer with Intel Core i5 or something similar or higher operating system</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>Working Hours:</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>20 hours per week</li>\n<li>Eastern Time</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>Compensation:</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>$7 per hour</li>\n<li>No benefits package included</li>\n</ul></strong></div>\n<h3><strong>Benefits</strong></h3>\n<div><div class=\"attachment-gallery attachment-gallery--6\"><strong>﻿﻿﻿﻿﻿﻿﻿﻿﻿﻿﻿﻿</strong></div></div>\n</div>\n</div><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
