  {
    "id": "himalayas-31214cc41a04",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "Junior Web Developer",
    "company": "",
    "location": "Argentina",
    "description": "<p><a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/community-sports-partners\">Community Sports Partners</a> is one of the largest and fastest-growing private youth sports operators in the GTA. We are dedicated to providing fun, engaging experiences that create lasting memories for the youth and families in our communities!</p><p>We are looking for a <strong>Junior Web Developer </strong>who is passionate about web design and development, with a primary focus on building high-converting landing pages and enhancing our website's front-end experience. This is an entry-level role ideal for candidates eager to gain experience in web development, particularly in UI/UX design and front-end technologies, with some exposure to back-end programming.</p><h3>Requirements</h3><ul>\n<li>Design and develop visually appealing, responsive landing pages and website components.</li>\n<li>Optimize front-end designs for speed, SEO, and mobile responsiveness.</li>\n<li>Implement UI/UX best practices to improve user experience and engagement.</li>\n<li>Collaborate with the design and marketing teams to align website updates with brand goals.</li>\n<li>Make minor back-end updates to support landing page functionality (basic PHP and SQL).</li>\n<li>Conduct A/B testing to analyze and improve user interactions.</li>\n<li>Debug and troubleshoot front-end issues to ensure smooth website performance.</li>\n<li>Stay up to date with the latest web design trends and technologies.</li>\n</ul><h3>Qualifications:</h3><h3>Required:</h3><h3>• 1-5 years professional experience.</h3><ul>\n<li>Basic experience with front-end technologies: HTML, CSS, JavaScript.</li>\n<li>Familiarity with responsive design and mobile-first development.</li>\n<li>Understanding of UI/UX principles and basic design concepts.</li>\n<li>Basic knowledge of back-end technologies such as PHP and SQL (for minor updates).</li>\n<li>Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.</li>\n<li>Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a remote environment.</li>\n</ul><h3>Nice to Have:</h3><ul>\n<li>Exposure to JavaScript frameworks (e.g., Vue.js, React).</li>\n<li>Familiarity with version control systems like Git.</li>\n<li>Experience with API integration (e.g., Stripe, Twilio, Brevo).</li>\n<li>Knowledge of SEO and web performance optimization.</li>\n<li>Previous experience in A/B testing and data-driven UI improvements.</li>\n</ul><h3>Benefits</h3><p>Compensation: Competitive based on experience</p><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
