  {
    "id": "himalayas-1a0eeefd03d4",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "Senior Frontend Engineer (Svelte)",
    "company": "",
    "location": "Ukraine",
    "description": "<p><strong>Senior Frontend Engineer (Svelte)  Full-Time, High-Impact Role</strong></p><p>Help us build the future of supply chain intelligence.</p><p>We're a small, fast-moving team building a next-generation supply chain AI platform. As a startup, we prioritize development speed and iteration. Creating solid and clean building blocks while delivering meaningful features is top of mind right now. We're well-funded and backed by prominent investors, founded by serial entrepreneurs who've previously raised hundreds of millions and built category-defining companies.</p><p>We need a <strong>Senior Frontend Engineer</strong> with a focus on <strong>Svelte or React</strong> who thrives in ambiguous environments, takes ownership, and can translate ideas into working interfaces, even when designs or specs are still in flux.</p><h3>What Youll Do:</h3><ul>\n<li><p>Work on frontend architecture and implementation</p></li>\n<li><p>Build dynamic, responsive UIs using Svelte (or React, if needed)</p></li>\n<li><p>Rapidly prototype features  sometimes before designs are finalized</p></li>\n<li><p>Collaborate closely with our designer and backend engineers</p></li>\n<li><p>Start with mock data or no data, then wire in backend integrations</p></li>\n<li><p>Improve development speed through smart tooling, CI, and test coverage</p></li>\n<li><p>Bring a product-minded approach to usability and interaction design</p></li>\n<li><p>Contribute to core architecture decisions for a system that works hand-in-hand with AI workflows</p></li>\n</ul><h3>You Should Have:</h3><ul>\n<li><p>5+ years of frontend development experience (ideally in start-up or fast-paced teams)</p></li>\n<li><p>Deep experience with Svelte or React (were leaning toward Svelte)</p></li>\n<li><p>Strong knowledge of component design, performance, and modern frontend practices</p></li>\n<li><p>Ability to move quickly from idea to prototype to production</p></li>\n<li><p>Self-driven, focused, and capable of working independently with minimal oversight</p></li>\n<li><p>Comfortable communicating and making decisions in a distributed team</p></li>\n</ul><h3>Bonus Points:</h3><ul>\n<li><p>Built or worked on AI-integrated, data-heavy, or real-time applications</p></li>\n<li><p>Experience setting up frontend CI/testing pipelines or using tools like Storybook</p></li>\n<li><p>Skilled in UI prototyping and fast idea validation</p></li>\n</ul><h3>Why Join Us?</h3><ul>\n<li><p>Youll have direct impact  this isnt a cog-in-the-machine role</p></li>\n<li><p>Work with a lean team where your decisions shape the product and culture</p></li>\n<li><p>Build fast, experiment often, and learn from real users</p></li>\n<li><p>High ownership with the flexibility to work where and when youre most productive</p></li>\n<li><p>Join early, grow with the company, and help define what great looks like</p></li>\n</ul><h3>To Apply</h3><p>Tell us about a UI or product you shipped quickly and are proud of  especially if it involved balancing speed with good design. Bonus if you can share a code snippet, link, or walkthrough.</p><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
