    "id": "himalayas-df421d966982",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "813 | Senior JavaScript Developer (Short term)",
    "company": "",
    "location": "Ukraine",
    "description": "<p><a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/intetics\">Intetics</a>, a leading global technology company providing custom software application development, distributed professional teams, software product quality assessment, and “all-things-digital” solutions, <strong>is looking for JavaScript Developer </strong>to enrich its team with a skilled professional to spread the company’s ideas, vision, content and messages.</p><h3>About the Project:</h3><p>The product is a web-based, artificially intelligent assessment and learning system. It uses adaptive questioning to quickly and accurately determine what a student knows or doesn’t know in a course.</p><p>Ground-breaking technology was developed by a team of software engineers, mathematicians, and cognitive scientists with the support of a multi-million-dollar grant from the National Science Foundation.</p><p>The system instructs the student on the topics he/she is most ready to learn. As a student works through a course, the system periodically reassesses the student to ensure that the issues learned are also retained. The learning courses are very complete in their topic coverage and avoid multiple-choice questions. A student who shows a high level of mastery of a system will be successful in the actual course he/she is taking.</p><p>The process is predictable and well-planned. SCRUM is used as a methodology.</p><h3>Responsibilities:</h3><p>Design, develop, debug, maintain, and testing of software applications;</p><p>Integrate new features and tools into the product, including features and tools developed by others, using such computer languages as JavaScript, HTML5, CSS, SVG, SQL, XML, JSON, and other general-purpose computer languages;</p><p>Review and accurate development against business requirements;</p><p>Follow established processes including SDLC, QA, performance optimization, and others</p><p>Defend code and applied patterns in code reviews;</p><p>Document technical changes and additions.</p><h3>Requirements</h3><ul>\n<li>3-5+ years of experience in commercial development  </li>\n<li>Strong background in pure JavaScript. </li>\n<li>Experience developing dynamic web applications utilizing JavaScript, HTML 5, CSS, SQL, and Ajax.</li>\n<li>Strong problem-solving and communication skills  </li>\n<li>Experience working on cross-browser platforms. </li>\n<li>Self-motivated, self-critical, very attentive to detail, self-learner.</li>\n<li>Upper-intermediate English level. </li>\n</ul><h3>Benefits</h3><ul>\n<li>Work in the exciting domain: e-Learning</li>\n<li>Business trips to Los Angeles (optionally)</li>\n<li>Work directly with the core development team</li>\n<li>Everyday English practice.</li>\n</ul><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
