    "id": "himalayas-854fd7fbca4e",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "Lead 2D JavaScript Game Developer-6+ Years",
    "company": "",
    "location": "India",
    "description": "<p><strong>Position: </strong><strong>Lead 2D JavaScript Game Developer</strong></p><h3>Remote: Yes</h3><h3>Start Date: Immediate</h3><h3>Duration: 3 months extendable</h3><h3>Number of positions: 1</h3><h3>Experience: 6+ Years</h3><h3>Working shift timing: India shift</h3><p>Selection Process: Technical Round followed by Practice Round. </p><h3>Job Description: Please find below</h3><ul>\n<li>highly skilled and experienced <strong>Lead 2D JavaScript Game Developer</strong> to<br>     join our team. </li>\n<li>As the Lead, you will not only be responsible for      developing interactive and<br>     engaging games using <strong>JavaScript,      HTML5, and CSS3</strong> but also for leading and      collaborating<br>     with other team members and cross-functional teams. The ideal candidate is      passionate about<br>     game development has a strong background in mathematics for collision      detection and<br>     velocity physics, and has experience in leading game development projects.<br><strong>Responsibilities:</strong><br><strong>1. Lead the game      development team:</strong><br>     o Provide technical leadership and guidance to the game development team.<br>     o Collaborate with artists, designers, and other developers to define game<br>     mechanics, features, and project requirements.<br>     o Mentor and provide support to junior developers, conducting code reviews      and<br>     providing constructive feedback.<br>     o Coordinate tasks and ensure timely delivery of high-quality game      projects.<br>     o Foster a collaborative and innovative work environment within the team.<br><strong>2. Develop      interactive and engaging games:</strong><br>     o Utilize <strong>JavaScript,      HTML5, and CSS3</strong> to develop games with high<br>     interactivity and engagement.<br>     o Implement mathematics algorithms for collision detection, physics<br>     simulations, and other game mechanics.<br>     o Optimize game performance for different platforms and devices.<br>     o Stay up-to-date with emerging game development technologies and<br>     techniques, and research and implement them as appropriate.<br>     o Integrate game environments with back-end systems and APIs      (nice-to-have).<br><strong>3. Collaborate with      cross-functional teams:</strong><br>     o Work closely with artists, designers, and other developers to create      visually<br>     appealing game assets and graphics.<br>     o Coordinate with back-end developers to integrate game functionality with<br>     server-side systems.<br>     o Collaborate with QA/testers to ensure high-quality game performance and<br>     resolve any issues.<br><br><strong>4. Ensure adherence      to best practices and industry standards:</strong><br>     o Stay up-to-date with industry trends, best practices, and advancements      in game<br>     development.<br>     o Apply software engineering principles and design patterns in game<br>     development.<br>     o Utilize version control systems (e.g., Git) and collaborative      development<br>     workflows.<br>     o Apply strong problem-solving and debugging skills to identify and      resolve<br>     issues.<br><strong>Requirements:</strong><br>     1. <strong>Bachelor of      Science in Computer Science</strong> or related field.<br>     2. Relevant coursework in <strong>Mathematics      for Game Developers and Physics for Game</strong><strong><br><strong>Developers.</strong></strong><br>     3. Minimum of <strong>6      years </strong>of experience as a JavaScript Game Developer or      similar role,<br>     with demonstrated experience in leading game development projects.<br>     4. Proficiency in <strong>JavaScript,      HTML5, CSS3, </strong><strong>Phaser and CreateJS -</strong> MUST HAVE</li>\n<li>5. Strong understanding of <strong>game development principles,</strong> best      practices, and<br>     mathematics for game development, including collision detection      algorithms, physics<br>     simulations for velocity and motion, vector and matrix operations, and      trigonometry<br>     and calculus for game mechanics.<br>     6. Experience with game engines/frameworks such as <strong>Phaser, CreateJS</strong>,      or similar.<br>     7. Good understanding of<strong> CSS3      and JS Animation frameworks like GreenSock</strong><br><strong>Animation Platform      (GSAP) or Anime.js</strong> to support 2D game development -      GOOD TO HAVE<br>     8. Knowledge of software engineering principles and design patterns.<br>     9. Familiarity with version control systems (e.g., Git) and collaborative      development<br>     workflows.<br>     10. Strong problem-solving and debugging skills.<br>     11. Effective communication and collaboration within multidisciplinary      teams.</li>\n</ul><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
