  {
    "id": "himalayas-7cb4283fd74c",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "Cisco Certified Systems Instructor (CCSI)",
    "company": "",
    "location": "India",
    "description": "<h3>About ITC Worldwide</h3><p>ITC Worldwide is a global leader in delivering high-impact technology training and consultancy services. We specialize in empowering professionals and organizations through expert-led instruction in enterprise platforms such as Cisco, Microsoft, AWS, and Red Hat. Our mission is to foster innovation and excellence through education. </p><h3>Role Overview</h3><p>We are seeking a highly skilled and certified Cisco Certified Systems Instructor (CCSI) to join our elite team of trainers. The ideal candidate will have deep expertise in Cisco technologies, a passion for teaching, and a proven ability to deliver engaging and effective training sessions to technical audiences across the globe. </p><h3>Key Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>Deliver official Cisco training courses to IT professionals, corporate clients, and academic institutions. </li></ul><ul><li>Facilitate hands-on labs, simulations, and interactive sessions to reinforce learning. </li></ul><ul><li>Customize training programs to meet specific client needs and learning objectives. </li></ul><ul><li>Stay current with Cisco technologies, certifications, and instructional standards. </li></ul><ul><li>Mentor learners pursuing Cisco certifications such as CCNA, CCNP, and CCIE. </li></ul><ul><li>Collaborate with curriculum developers to enhance course materials and lab environments. </li></ul><ul><li>Conduct assessments and evaluations to measure training effectiveness. </li></ul><ul><li>Support marketing and sales teams in promoting Cisco training offerings. </li></ul><ul><li>Maintain CCSI status through continuous learning, certification, and compliance with Ciscos Instructor Kit membership. </li></ul><h3>Required Skills and Qualifications</h3><ul><li>Valid Cisco Certified Systems Instructor (CCSI) credential. </li></ul><ul><li>Minimum of 710 years of experience in networking and Cisco technologies. </li></ul><ul><li>Proven track record of delivering Cisco certification training (e.g., CCNA, CCNP, CCIE). </li></ul><ul><li>Strong understanding of Cisco technologies including routing, switching, security, wireless, and collaboration. </li></ul><ul><li>Excellent presentation, communication, and interpersonal skills. </li></ul><ul><li>Experience in instructional design and adult learning methodologies. </li></ul><ul><li>Ability to adapt training delivery to different learning styles and technical levels. </li></ul><ul><li>Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail. </li></ul><ul><li>Willingness to travel for on-site training engagements. </li></ul><ul><li>Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field. </li></ul><h3>Preferred Skills</h3><ul><li>Additional Cisco certifications (e.g., CCNP Security, CCIE Enterprise). </li></ul><ul><li>Experience with Cisco platforms such as Meraki, DNA Center, and SD-WAN. </li></ul><ul><li>Familiarity with virtual labs and e-learning platforms. </li></ul><ul><li>Ability to create interactive and multimedia training materials. </li></ul><ul><li>Knowledge of DevOps and cloud integration with Cisco technologies. </li></ul><ul><li>Experience in course development, examination, and assessment. </li></ul><h3>Professional Development</h3><p>As part of ITC Worldwide, youll gain access to continuous learning opportunities, collaborate with top-tier instructors, and contribute to shaping the future of networking education. </p><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
