  {
    "id": "himalayas-d710c781fc94",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "Maintenance Instructor (Vacante interna)",
    "company": "",
    "location": "United States",
    "description": "<p>The Maintenance Instructor is responsible for delivering high-quality technical training to maintenance personnel, with a primary focus on safety. This role ensures that maintenance personnel are well-versed in the company policies and procedures and equipped with the necessary skills and knowledge to maintain and repair aircraft and aviation equipment safely and in compliance with industry and regulatory standards. The instructor will develop, deliver, and assess training programs that foster efficient, compliant, and high-quality maintenance operations across the organization.</p><p>﻿<strong>KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES: </strong>﻿</p><h3>Training Development</h3><ul>\n<li>Designs and updates comprehensive training programs, presentations, course materials, and assessments to cover essential skills and align with industry standards and company policies.</li>\n<li>Ensures all materials are prepared to facilitate effective learning and skill development for maintenance technicians.</li>\n<li>Provide expert guidance in identifying the root causes of issues arising from SMS and quality assurance events and ensure these are addressed through tailored remedial training programs.</li>\n</ul><ul><li>Collaborate with safety, quality, and operational teams to define specific training objectives aimed at rectifying deficiencies, improving compliance, and enhancing operational performance.</li></ul><h3>Training Delivery</h3><ul>\n<li>Conducts   engaging classroom and practical training sessions on aircraft systems,   maintenance techniques, regulatory requirements, safety protocols, and other   relevant topics.</li>\n<li>Uses   interactive methods to enhance trainee understanding and retention of   technical information.</li>\n</ul><h3>Performance Assessment</h3><ul>\n<li>Assesses   and identifies training needs by evaluating each technician's knowledge base   and skill level, tailoring training objectives to bridge gaps and support   growth in areas requiring improvement.</li>\n<li>Provides   constructive, targeted feedback to guide technicians in acquiring the   expertise needed for proficiency and career advancement, fostering a culture   of continuous learning and skill enhancement.</li>\n<li>Works with technicians to create individual   development plans that outline clear steps for skill-building, setting   achievable milestones to reach industry standards and support long-term   career goals.</li>\n</ul><h3>Career Plan Development</h3><ul>\n<li>Collaborate   with maintenance management to identify career growth opportunities for   personnel based on performance, skills, and career aspirations.</li>\n<li>Provide   mentorship and guidance to help individuals advance their knowledge and   qualifications.</li>\n<li>Assist   in creating tailored development plans that align with the organization's   needs.</li>\n<li>Promote   a culture of continuous learning and professional growth within the   maintenance department.</li>\n</ul><h3>Continuous   improvement </h3><ul>\n<li>Collects   and analyses feedback from training participants to assess the effectiveness   of training materials, delivery methods, and overall impact.</li>\n<li>Uses   feedback to refine training content, methodologies, and instructional   approaches to ensure continuous improvement and alignment with the evolving   needs of the technicians and industry standards.</li>\n</ul><h3>Regulatory   and Other</h3><p>Safeguard the company by   ensuring adherence to all relevant policies, regulatory requirements, and   industry standards within the instructor's specific area and across the   organization. This proactive approach mitigates the risk of high-risk audit   findings, regulatory violations, and potential financial or reputational   damage.<br><br><strong>Functions and Responsibilities in relation to SMS are:  </strong></p><ul>\n<li>Comply   with the Policies, Objectives and Requirements of the Operational Safety   Management System.  </li>\n<li>Actively   participate in the Operational Safety Reporting System.  </li>\n<li>Inform   the Operational Safety and Risk Management of the dangers, accidents,   incidents, unsafe acts, violations, deviations and unsafe conditions that are   generated in the operation and maintenance work. </li>\n<li>Address   and establish action plans to close non-conformities generated during the   different audits scheduled by internal auditors. </li>\n<li>Receive,   read and understand the information provided by Operational Safety and act in   accordance with the given guidelines.  </li>\n<li>Attend   and approve the Operational Safety Instruction. </li>\n<li>Receive   and answer the Operational Safety surveys designed by the Operational Safety   and Risk Management.</li>\n</ul><p>﻿<strong>QUALIFICATIONS, EXPERIENCE, &amp; SKILLS: </strong>﻿</p><ul>\n<li>Diploma or degree in Aviation Maintenance, Aeronautical Engineering, or a related field.</li>\n<li>Minimum of 5 years of hands-on experience as an aviation maintenance technician, with 2+ years in an instructional or training role.</li>\n<li>Relevant aviation maintenance licenses. Instructor certifications are an asset.</li>\n<li>In-depth knowledge of aircraft systems, maintenance practices, tools, equipment, and safety regulations.</li>\n<li>Strong verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to convey complex technical concepts in an understandable manner.</li>\n<li>Proficiency with training software and tools, including Learning Management Systems (LMS) and virtual training platforms.</li>\n</ul><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
