  {
    "id": "himalayas-40192d9171d3",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "MTT Instructor",
    "company": "",
    "location": "United States",
    "description": "<div>\n<p><img></p>\n<h3>About <a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/owt-global\">OWT Global</a>\n</h3>\n<p>Founded in 2010 and headquartered in Tampa, FL, <a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/owt-global\">OWT Global</a> is an SBA Small Business delivering reliable, operationally proven expertise and mission-focused support to the U.S. Government, industry partners, and commercial clients. Recognized as a Top Workplace by the Tampa Bay Times from 2022–2026, <a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/owt-global\">OWT Global</a> specializes in deployed Field Services, Engineering Support, RDT&amp;E, Technical Program &amp; Project Management, logistics, maintenance, training, and operational support for advanced technologies and mission systems across Unmanned Systems (UxS), Command, Control, Communications, Computers, Cyber, Intelligence, Surveillance, and Reconnaissance (C5ISR), and Air Domain Awareness &amp; Defense (ADAD) mission areas. Our unique services-first and vendor-agnostic approach provides customers with dedication, quality, flexibility, and reliability from a partner that prioritizes mission success above all else. <a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/owt-global\">OWT Global</a> proudly supports the DoW SkillBridge Program, helping transitioning service members move into civilian careers. With a workforce comprised of more than 90% veterans from the very operational communities we support, our team brings unmatched mission understanding, operational experience, and technical expertise to every effort.</p>\n<h3>Position Overview</h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/owt-global\">OWT Global</a> LLC is seeking MTT Instructors to deliver contractor-provided Mobile Training Team services in support of JIATF-401 Counter-small Unmanned Aircraft System (C-sUAS) training operations. This requirement includes a baseline of 30 instructors with the ability to surge an additional 15 instructors. Instructors will project Joint C-UAS University (JCU)-standardized instruction and advanced tactical capabilities directly to individual installations, supporting Domestic Shield operational training, JIATF-401 new personnel onboarding, Base Defense Operations Center (BDOC) training, and Joint Force C-sUAS training integration while preserving full operational uptime.</p>\n<h3>Key Responsibilities</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliver formal and informal C-sUAS instruction in accordance with JCU-validated doctrine and approved Programs of Instruction.</li>\n<li>Conduct classroom, practical, and field training events that project JCU-standardized content to operational units and installations.</li>\n<li>Prepare lesson plans, training aids, and evaluation materials aligned with current C-sUAS threats and defensive tactics.</li>\n<li>Assess student and unit performance against operational C-sUAS standards and document results.</li>\n<li>Maintain instructor proficiency and currency in Counter-sUAS systems, tactics, and Joint C-UAS University standards.</li>\n<li>Support surge operations by rapidly expanding instructional capacity to meet peak Domestic Shield and installation training demand.</li>\n<li>Coordinate with JCU Cadre, the MTT Synchronization Cell, Curriculum Integration Specialist, and Training Operations staff.</li>\n<li>Uphold safety, security, and operational standards during all training activities.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Required Qualifications</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Bachelor’s degree preferred or equivalent military/technical experience.</li>\n<li>5+ years of relevant instructional or operational experience, preferably in Counter-UAS, air defense, base defense, or related mission areas.</li>\n<li>Prior military instructor experience (Army Instructor Badge, Marine Combat Instructor, or equivalent) strongly preferred.</li>\n<li>Active Secret clearance; U.S. Citizen.</li>\n<li>Ability to travel extensively and support both CONUS and OCONUS MTT missions.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Desired Skills &amp; Experience</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Direct experience delivering Mobile Training Team or expeditionary C-sUAS training.</li>\n<li>Familiarity with Joint C-UAS University doctrine, Domestic Shield, or JIATF-401 training constructs.</li>\n<li>Strong presentation, coaching, and classroom management skills.</li>\n<li>Ability to surge and operate effectively in high-tempo training environments.</li>\n<li>Strongly prefer ability to operate Group 1 and Group 2 UAS</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Clearance &amp; Citizenship</h3>\n<ul><li>Active Secret clearance required; U.S. Citizen.</li></ul>\n<h3>Location</h3>\n<ul><li>Remote</li></ul>\n<h3>What We Offer</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Competitive compensation</li>\n<li>Comprehensive benefits starting day one (medical, dental, vision)</li>\n<li>401(k) with generous company match and immediate vesting</li>\n<li>Paid Time Off (PTO) and Federal holidays</li>\n<li>Opportunity to support meaningful missions impacting national security</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Benefits</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Comprehensive Coverage: Health, Dental, and Vision insurance through UnitedHealthcare with a 50% employer contribution.</li>\n<li>Insurance Protection: Competitive short- and long-term disability, basic life insurance, and Workers’ Compensation coverage.</li>\n<li>Retirement Plans: Traditional and Roth 401(k) options with a 4% employer match through Principal with immediate vesting.</li>\n<li>Paid Time Off: Generous PTO, including 160 hours of PTO and 11 days of paid holiday leave.</li>\n</ul>\n</div><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
