    "id": "himalayas-af0c65f37922",
    "source": "Himalayas",
    "title": "IntelliJ Plugins Engineer",
    "company": "",
    "location": "Germany, India, United Kingdom, United States",
    "description": "<p>We are #VLteam - tech enthusiasts constantly striving for growth. The team is our foundation, that's why we care the most about the friendly atmosphere, a lot of self-development opportunities and good working conditions (yes, that also means attractive salaries). Trust and autonomy are two essential qualities that drive our performance. We simply believe in the idea of ​​“measuring outcomes, not hours”. Join us &amp; see for yourself! </p><p>We are seeking a Senior Engineer to work on IDEs such as PHPStorm, RubyMine, or core plugins within the JetBrains ecosystem. Your role will entail implementing new features, maintaining clean and testable code, reviewing contributions, and collaborating with a passionate team. You will have opportunities to influence the plugin’s or IDE’s direction and improve the experience for many developers.</p><h3>Requirements</h3><h4><strong>IDE Engineer (Senior)</strong></h4><p>Details : IDE Engineer (Senior) - Careers <a href=\"https://himalayas.app/companies/virtuslab\">VirtusLab</a></p><h3>Required skills:</h3><p><strong>Kotlin or Java - </strong>Advanced</p><p><strong>Multithreaded Programming - </strong>Advanced</p><p><strong>Plugin Development (IntelliJ) - </strong>Nice to have</p><p><strong>Java Swing - </strong>Nice to have</p><p><strong>Kotlin coroutines - </strong>Nice to have</p><p><strong>English - </strong>Advanced</p><h3>What we expect in general</h3><ul>\n<li><p>5+ years of experience in Kotlin or Java development</p></li>\n<li><p>Good understanding of concurrency, preferably Kotlin Coroutines</p></li>\n<li><p>Experience with extending IDEs or any GUI Java frameworks</p></li>\n<li><p>Experience with working on compiler or code analysis tools is a plus</p></li>\n<li><h3>English at B2 level or higher</h3></li>\n<li><p>Passion for improving developer tools and open-source software</p></li>\n</ul><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
